[ti:Day 18]

[00:00.00]diverge 例 There is a concern that euro zone economies may diverge when some regions are more affected than others by shocks. 有人 担心当一些地区比其他地区受冲击的影响更大 时，欧元区经济体可能会产生分歧。
[00:15.79]compatible 例 This software is not compatible with your hardware. 这个软件与你的硬件不兼容。
[00:24.22]computerise 例 Their decision flve years ago to computerise the company is now paying dividends. 五年前他们作出的给公司配计算机的 决定现在正产生效益。
[00:36.63]incidental 例 His success in career is not incidental at all. 他事业上取得的成功绝非偶然。
[00:44.30]juxtapose 例 Be sure to juxtapose your solutions so as to finish the task in the easiest and most efflcient way. 一定要对比你的几个解决方案，确 保用最简单、有效的方法完成任务。
[00:58.25]aversion 例 Risk aversion is one of the biggest factors driving allocation. 风险厌恶是推动资产配置的最 大因素之一。
[01:07.91]expectancy 例 All products have a life expectancy. 所有商 品都有预期使用年限。
[01:14.34]dock 例 The dockers disburdened the merchandise at the dock and then left. 码头工人把货物卸在 码头上后就离开了。
[01:23.70]opaque 例 The institution has been opaque about its flnances over the years. 此机构多年来都不曾对 外公布过它的财务状况。
[01:33.35]upshot 例 The upshot of the talks is that both sides build up a partnership. 会谈的结果是双方建立了 合作关系。
[01:42.70]bounce 例 The fact that her check bounced left her at a loss. 支票被拒的事实使她不知所措。
[01:50.06]engender 例 Company love is possibly engendered due to a long-term work relationship. 长期的工作关 系可能导致办公室恋情。
[02:01.10]bulky 例 These systems are usually bulky and difficult to use. 这些系统往往非常庞大，难以使 用。
[02:08.92]superiority 例 The company has established absolute superiority over its opponents. 跟其对手相比， 该公司已形成绝对的优势。
[02:19.95]codetermination 例 The funds may, upon the codetermination of the owners, be used for maintaining such common parts as elevators and water tanks. 经业主共同决定，这些资金可以用于电梯、水箱 等公共部分的维修。
[02:38.66]hire 例 It's obvious that an employer cannot afford to hire incapable workers. 很显然，一个雇主不 可能出钱雇用没有能力的员工。
[02:48.62]underpaid 例 The hard-working salesman never complained of being underpaid. 那名销售员工 作勤恳，却从来没有抱怨过薪酬过低。
[02:58.58]espionage 例 Only the big boss knows the detailed plan to protect against espionage. 为了防范商业间 谍，只有大老板知道详细计划。
[03:09.32]denounce 例 Many web users strongly denounce some e-commerce sites for selling diluted cosmetics. 许多网友强烈谴责一些电子商务网站 销售稀释后的化妆品。
[03:22.04]well-being 例 A positive corporate culture can contribute to both the company's development and the well-being of the employees. 积极向上的企业 文化有助于公司的发展，也有利于员工的健康。
[03:38.75]zeal 例 To finish the project on time, they plunged into their work with a determined zeal. 为了按 时完成项目，他们拼命地工作。
[03:50.09]breach 例 The snooty envoy seems to regard meeting anyone below the prime minister as a breach of protocol. 这位高傲自大的使节似乎认为会见低 于首相级别的任何人都是违反外交礼节的。
[04:03.58]consolidate 例 The three colleges will consolidate and form a bigger university next year. 明年，那三 所学院将合并，组建成一所规模更大的大学。
[04:15.23]competency 例 In order to establish the supply inventory, resources must be classified by both competency and skill. 为了建立供应详细目录， 必须按照能力和技能对资源进行分类。
[04:30.26]inflow 例 Extra capital inflow for the start-up company will be forthcoming as planned. 这家 新创公司的额外资本流入将按计划到来。
[04:41.45]decertify 例 Under the current rules, if the authority wants to decertify a lab, it must revoke the accreditation of the entire institution. 在当前的 规定下，如果当局想取消一个实验室，就必须撤 销对整个机构的认证。
[04:59.38]embroil 例 Do your best to avoid our products being embroiled in any dispute. 尽量避免让我们的产 品陷入任何纷争。
[05:09.04]shakeout 例 A shakeout in America's economy is unavoidable. 美国经济的衰退是不可避免的。
[05:16.71]zoom 例 House prices suddenly zoomed at the beginning of this year. 今年年初，房价突然急速 上升。
[05:25.14]span 例 It takes about fifteen minutes to span the river. 横穿这条河大约需要15分钟。
[05:32.19]coup 例 Getting the contract was quite a coup. 把合
[05:37.86]indignant 例 He was very indignant with his boss's unjust treatment. 他因老板对自己的不公正待遇 感到非常愤慨。
[05:46.60]perennial 例 The cosmetics of this brand are a perennial favourite. 这个品牌的化妆品一直很受欢迎。
[05:55.18]unravel 例 The investors' focus remains on whether the government will unravel the fiscal cliff problem. 投资者的焦点停留在政府是否能够解决 财政悬崖问题。
[06:08.67]chart 例 They tried to chart the sea area between Norway and Denmark. 他们努力想要绘制出挪威 与丹麦之间的海域图。
[06:17.26]abundance 例 Such inferior products are available in abundance on the market. 市场上有很多这样的 劣质产品。
[06:27.22]exodus 例 It's said that we're facing the exodus of foreign capital from real estate market. 据说我 们正面临着外资从房地产市场的大批撤离。
[06:38.87]consign 例 We will consign the goods to our clients by express. 我们将通过快递把货物寄给我们的客 户。
[06:46.69]apportion 例 This helps to apportion the responsibility to the correct development team for detailed analysis. 这有助于将任务分配到正确的开发团 队，以便进行详细分析。
[07:01.10]stumble 例 With rising labor costs, China's economic growth could stumble. 随着劳动力成本的增加， 中国的经济增长可能会面临搁浅的危险。
[07:10.76]facsimile 例 Along with the network popularisation, the digital facsimile has emerged due to the requirements of the times. 随着网络的普及，数 字传真应运而生。
[07:26.70]overtake 例 In our department, nobody can overtake him in creative design. 我们部门没人能在创意设 计上超过他。
[07:36.21]openness 例 If the cooperation is to succeed, we'll need openness on both sides. 合作的成功需要我们双 方坦诚相待。
[07:46.33]balloon 例 Trade deflcits have ballooned. 贸易逆差急剧 扩大。
[07:51.69]discern 例 Sometimes you cannot discern the truth of an event from a newspaper report. 有时候，从 报纸的报道看不出事情的真实性。
[08:02.57]fulfil 例 Our solution will fulfil these requirements, but it is not necessarily constrained by them. 我们的解决方案将满足这些需求，但是并不一定 要被它们所约束。
[08:15.60]equate 例 To some extent, the goods of big brands can be equated to ones with good quality. 从 某种程度上来说，大品牌的商品可以被认为是高 质量的商品。
[08:26.80]extension 例 An extention of three days will be made immediately for your visit card to our company in case we get your request for a leave postponed. 收到您延迟离开的请求后，您在我公 司的参观证将即刻延长三天。
[08:45.50]entrant 例 We're only an entrant firm now. 本公司刚成 立不久。
[08:50.71]compact 例 They remain at loggerheads over the contents of a new flscal compact. 他们在新财 政契约的内容上仍存在很大的分歧。
[09:00.83]sock 例 He has managed to sock an enormous sum of money. 他已经攒了一大笔钱。
